  "prefLabel": "Mec 102.14 Fuel gas trainee",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Mec 102.14 “Fuel gas trainee” means “fuel gas trainee” as defined in RSA 153:27, VIII, namely, “any person engaged in the process of meeting the licensing requirements of this subdivision, who shall work under the direct supervision of a licensed fuel gas fitter in the repair or installation of inside and outside piping from a gas meter or first stage regulator, and the repair or installation of residential and nonresidential fuel gas appliances and equipment, including but not limited to heating equipment systems, hot water heating systems, domestic appliances, or hearth equipment systems utilizing liquefied propane gas or natural gas.”\n\nSource. #10798, eff 3-18-15; ss by #13483, eff 1-9-23 (formerly Saf-Mec 102.09) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Mec 100); #14408, eff 10-17-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/mec100.html"
